---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site.js";
---
<Base title="Downloads">
	<div class="post">
		<h2 class="section-title">Downloads</h2>
		<div class="box">
			<p>Skyline Tower needs some extra content (maps, models, sounds and textures) to look right. It's all on the Steam Workshop, so there's nothing to install by hand.</p>

			<h3>Step 1: Subscribe to the collection</h3>
			<p>Open our Workshop collection and click <b>Subscribe to all</b>. Steam downloads everything and keeps it up to date for you.</p>
			<p class="center"><a class="btn btn-blue" href={site.links.workshop}>Workshop Collection</a></p>

			<h3>Step 2: Mount Counter-Strike: Source (recommended)</h3>
			<p>Some maps and props use CS:S content. If you own it, mount it from the Garry's Mod main menu (the controller icon at the bottom right). Without it, you'll see some pink-and-black checkerboards.</p>

			<h3>Step 3: Join!</h3>
			<p>Click <b>Connect to Skyline</b> at the top of any page, or open your console in Garry's Mod and type:</p>
			<p class="center"><code>connect {site.servers[0].address}</code></p>

			<h3>Why Workshop?</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>It's quick, compressed, and needs no extra programs.</li>
				<li>Updates download automatically.</li>
				<li>It's tied to your Steam account, so it comes back if you reinstall.</li>
				<li>It works on Windows, macOS and Linux.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</Base>
